
 What is the primary goal of the Distance Vector Routing Algorithm?
a: To find the shortest path between two nodes
b: To determine the fastest network protocol
c: To establish direct communication between all nodes
d: To assign IP addresses dynamically
Which type of information does each node maintain in Distance Vector Routing?
a: Only its own IP address
b: Cost estimates to all other nodes
c: A list of all network devices
d: The entire network topology
How do nodes exchange routing information in Distance Vector Routing?
a: By broadcasting their full network topology
b: By exchanging distance vectors with neighbors
c: By sending data packets to all nodes
d: By maintaining a central routing table
Which mathematical equation is used to update a node's distance vector?
a: Dₓ(y) = max{c(x, v) - Dᵥ(y)}
b: Dₓ(y) = min{c(x, v) + Dᵥ(y)}
c: Dₓ(y) = sum{c(x, v) * Dᵥ(y)}
d: Dₓ(y) = Dᵥ(y) / c(x, v)
